12:1 W [unused-variable] Unused variable 'loose'. Prefix with '_' if intentional.
15:1 W [suppression] kupcad:disable-next-line self-subtraction hides nothing here; remove it
17:1 W [suppression] kupcad:disable-next-line names no rule 'unused-varable' (`kupcad check --help` lists them)
18:1 W [suppression] unknown directive 'kupcad:disable-nextline' (use disable-next-line, disable-line or disable)
19:1 W [suppression] kupcad:disable-line must name the rules it hides
--- after --fix (1 fixed) ---
# kupcad:disable param-order -- this file reads params before defining them
early = param(:width)
width = param(:width, default: 10)

# kupcad:disable-next-line unused-variable
spare = 1
also_spare = 2 # kupcad:disable-line unused-variable -- kept for the next revision

# Hides the next line only: `loose` is still reported.
# kupcad:disable-next-line unused-variable
hidden = 3
_loose = 4

# A directive that hides nothing, a rule that doesn't exist, a mistyped directive.
# kupcad:disable-next-line self-subtraction
part = cube(width + early)
# kupcad:disable-next-line unused-varable
# kupcad:disable-nextline unused-variable
# kupcad:disable-line

# Two rules hidden by one directive, listed with a comma and with a space
spent = part - part # kupcad:disable-line unused-variable, self-subtraction
spent_too = part - part # kupcad:disable-line unused-variable self-subtraction
part
